  "title": "We Voted to End Foreign Wars — So Why Are We Paying for Another One?",
  "slug": "we-voted-to-end-foreign-wars-so-why-are-we-paying-for-another-one",
  "category": "Politics & Power",
  "subcategory": "America First vs. Both Parties",
  "image": "assets/blog/post1.jpg",
  "paragraphs": [
   "Let me tell you something. We did not vote for this.",
   "In 2024, Americans went to the polls and said the same thing in every state, in every rural county, at every kitchen table: no more foreign wars. We were done sending our sons and our money to fight in places most people couldn't find on a map. That's what we voted for.",
   "And then what happened? We went to war with Iran. Not because Iran attacked us. Because Washington decided — again — that another country's problems were worth American lives and American dollars.",
   "Here's what it's cost you, and I want you to sit with it. The Strait of Hormuz got choked off, and gas prices climbed while your paycheck didn't. Diesel went up, which means everything that moves on a truck — your groceries, your feed, your fuel — went up right along with it. The military burned through munitions we spent years and billions building, weapons we may need to defend our own country. And now there's talk of a reconstruction deal. I'm assuming that bill lands on the American taxpayer, because it always does.",
   "We bomb it. Then we rebuild it. With your money. And nobody in Washington asked you.",
   "You want to know the part that makes my blood boil? They'll tell you this was about keeping you safe. Same thing they said about every war that drained this country and buried our kids. Meanwhile the people who voted to send the bombs sleep just fine, and the people who pay for them — you — get told to be grateful.",
   "I spent my time in Congress fighting this exact thing. Foreign wars dressed up as necessity, sold to a public that already said no. I'll keep saying it now that I'm out, louder, because there's no leadership left to muzzle me.",
   "We are the freest country in the world, and we can't even keep our own government from spending us into another war we didn't ask for. That's not freedom. That's a racket.",
   "So here's what I want you to do. Don't take my word for any of it. Do your own research. Look at what this cost, look at who profited, and look at who's rebuilding what we just destroyed. Then ask yourself if a single person in Washington asked your permission. They didn't. They never do. And that's exactly why we can't stop paying attention."
  ],
