  "title": "I Backed the Movement. Then It Went to War Without Us.",
  "slug": "i-backed-the-movement-then-it-went-to-war-without-us",
  "category": "Politics & Power",
  "subcategory": "America First vs. Both Parties",
  "image": "assets/blog/post2.jpg",
  "paragraphs": [
   "I helped build the America First movement. I fought for it, I took the arrows for it, and I meant every word. So let me be honest with you about what it's like to watch the people you stood with turn around and do the exact thing you all promised you never would.",
   "We went to war with Iran. And I said no — loudly, publicly, and to the people who used to call me an ally. Because we did not vote for this. In 2024, Americans said it as clearly as they've ever said anything: no more foreign wars. No more American money and American lives spent on other countries' fights. That was the promise. That was the whole point.",
   "Then the bombs fell anyway. And when I said what half the country was thinking — that this betrayed the exact voters who put these people in power — I went from ally to enemy overnight. I've been called a traitor by people who used to put me on their stage.",
   "So let me tell you how I define a traitor, because it isn't the person who keeps her word after everyone else breaks theirs. A traitor is someone who serves foreign countries and themselves before the American people. By that definition, I know exactly who the traitors are, and it isn't me.",
   "Here's what this taught me, and it's the most important political lesson I've got. America First was never supposed to be a team you join. It's a test you apply — to every politician, every party, every single time. Does this serve the American people, or does it serve somebody else? The minute you turn it into a loyalty club, it stops meaning anything, because the people at the top will happily wave the flag while they do the opposite of what it stands for.",
   "I'm not on a team anymore, and I'm not interested in one. I answer to the same people I always have — the families who work, pay, and get lied to, and who were promised no more wars and got another one.",
   "They can call me whatever they want. I've been called worse by better. What they can't do is make me pretend I didn't see what I saw.",
   "So apply the test yourself, to everyone, including the people you like. Do your own research on who actually kept their word and who folded the moment it counted. That's the only loyalty ever worth anything — loyalty to the truth, not the team."
  ],
